# Language Policy: English Only in Code & Comments

Never mix French and English in the repository.

- **English Only (Mandatory)**: All source code, identifiers, inline comments, docstrings (`///`, `/** */`), test descriptions, error messages, commit messages, PR titles/bodies, `GLOSSARY.md`, `AGENTS.md`, ADRs (`docs/adr/`), and technical specifications (`docs/specs/`) MUST be written strictly in English.
- **No Bilingual Mixing**: Do not mix French and English in the same file, comment, or glossary entry (e.g., avoid `Allowed: AbilityScore, score de caractéristique`).
- **End-User Documentation Exception**: French is reserved exclusively for dedicated end-user documentation or localization files when explicitly requested later.

## Examples

```rust
// BAD (French or mixed French/English comment)
// Calcule le modificateur de caractéristique (ability modifier)
pub fn ability_modifier(score: i32) -> i32 {
    (score - 10).div_euclid(2)
}

// GOOD (English only)
/// Computes the standard D&D 5e ability modifier: `floor((score - 10) / 2)`.
pub fn ability_modifier(score: i32) -> i32 {
    (score - 10).div_euclid(2)
}
```
